Where are you gonna get your shit from.
sweetheart?

756
00:46:46.887 --> 00:46:48.807
Only friends and family get the discount.

757
00:46:50.683 --> 00:46:51.683
Alex!

758
00:46:57.773 --> 00:46:59.363
[Melody] It's good to see you again.

759
00:47:00.735 --> 00:47:02.395
What's your pleasure today. honey?

760
00:47:06.198 --> 00:47:07.198
[stifled sob]

761
00:47:08.034 --> 00:47:09.034
Sweetie...

762
00:47:14.707 --> 00:47:15.707
Come here.

763
00:47:17.501 --> 00:47:19.421
Come here. It's okay.

764
00:47:21.672 --> 00:47:23.672
[sobbing]

765
00:47:24.175 --> 00:47:25.215
It's gonna be okay.

766
00:47:26.052 --> 00:47:28.682
[Alex] <i>I don't think</i>
<i>I'll ever forget that little kid's face.</i>

767
00:47:29.972 --> 00:47:31.522
I'm sure he won't forget mine.

768
00:47:33.434 --> 00:47:36.854
After that. I didn't get the discount.
which is why the payments went up.

769
00:47:37.396 --> 00:47:41.066
He never blackmailed me.
He never said a thing about anything.

770
00:47:41.150 --> 00:47:42.230
Wait. so are you...

771
00:47:43.110 --> 00:47:44.990
Are you using now. or are you clean?

772
00:47:45.863 --> 00:47:46.913
Nobody's clean.

773
00:47:48.407 --> 00:47:51.487
- Alex. you don't have to go.
- Yeah. Well. I'm not going to stay.

774
00:47:52.328 --> 00:47:53.498
I don't want you to...

775
00:47:56.582 --> 00:47:57.942
I don't want you to hurt yourself.

776
00:47:59.001 --> 00:48:00.961
Yeah. I've run out of ways to do that.

777
00:48:08.094 --> 00:48:10.104
[Clay sighing]

778
00:48:18.604 --> 00:48:20.364
Do you think I'm a sad. skinny kid?

779
00:48:24.026 --> 00:48:25.066
Ah...

780
00:48:25.653 --> 00:48:28.493
I think you are a lean...

781
00:48:29.824 --> 00:48:32.284
but right-sized...

782
00:48:33.452 --> 00:48:34.662
very handsome.

783
00:48:35.454 --> 00:48:36.794
very complicated kid.

784
00:48:42.711 --> 00:48:43.711
I'll take it.

785
00:48:48.968 --> 00:48:50.428
["Funeral" playing]

786
00:48:50.553 --> 00:48:51.763
[door closing]

787
00:48:54.140 --> 00:48:55.810
How's... how's Alex?

788
00:48:58.352 --> 00:48:59.352
Messed up.

789
00:49:01.188 --> 00:49:02.268
But aren't we all?

790
00:49:04.066 --> 00:49:07.776
You know. I really didn't think
he had anything to do with Bryce. but...

791
00:49:10.573 --> 00:49:13.243
drugs of any kind. man. they fuck you up.

792
00:49:14.034 --> 00:49:15.034
Yeah.

793
00:49:18.747 --> 00:49:22.077
I'll have you know.
the gun is gone for good.

794
00:49:25.212 --> 00:49:26.712
Awesome. Thanks.

795
00:49:30.885 --> 00:49:32.505
You seem awfully dark tonight.

796
00:49:35.347 --> 00:49:36.427
How are you not?

797
00:49:39.852 --> 00:49:40.852
I guess I am.

798
00:49:43.481 --> 00:49:46.321
But I'm alive.
so I figure I'm ahead of the game.

799
00:49:46.525 --> 00:49:47.525
[scoffs]

800
00:49:49.278 --> 00:49:50.278
Right.

801
00:49:52.740 --> 00:49:55.530
I don't want to believe
someone we know killed Bryce.

802
00:49:57.244 --> 00:49:59.664
But it seems like
everyone we know had a reason.

803
00:50:00.748 --> 00:50:02.168
Everyone's got their shit.

804
00:50:07.004 --> 00:50:08.004
Yes.

805
00:50:10.799 --> 00:50:15.639
<i>♪ Jesus Christ I'm so blue all the time ♪</i>

806
00:50:16.055 --> 00:50:19.555
<i>♪ And that's just how I feel ♪</i>

807
00:50:19.642 --> 00:50:25.982
<i>♪ Always have and I always will ♪</i>

808
00:50:26.482 --> 00:50:30.282
<i>♪ I always have and I always will ♪</i>

809
00:50:47.753 --> 00:50:49.003
[footsteps approaching]

810
00:50:49.421 --> 00:50:50.801
[Bryce] Yeah. it's coke.

811
00:50:54.718 --> 00:50:56.968
You ever tried it before?
I've got some more.

812
00:50:58.222 --> 00:50:59.272
No. thank you.

813
00:51:00.808 --> 00:51:04.478
I offered to help the maids
prepare the study.

814
00:51:05.229 --> 00:51:06.229
Your grandfa...

815
00:51:06.313 --> 00:51:09.733
I'm sure you've had it before.
You're a city girl. You're all fancy.

816
00:51:10.609 --> 00:51:14.199
Your grandfather plans
to receive some old friends tomorrow.

817
00:51:14.280 --> 00:51:16.820
Well. let's hope they don't notice
the missing bourbon.

818
00:51:19.285 --> 00:51:20.285
Cheers.

819
00:51:22.538 --> 00:51:25.328
You look tired.
Perhaps you should get some sleep.

820
00:51:25.416 --> 00:51:27.746
He's a piece of work. my grandfather.
isn't he?

821
00:51:28.961 --> 00:51:29.961
He's...

822
00:51:31.380 --> 00:51:33.380
an interesting man.

823
00:51:35.134 --> 00:51:36.134
He's a...

824
00:51:37.011 --> 00:51:40.391
racist. homophobic. angry piece of shit.

825
00:51:46.103 --> 00:51:47.613
My dad bought a new house.

826
00:51:49.398 --> 00:51:51.978
Same fucking neighborhood as the old one.

827
00:51:53.527 --> 00:51:56.447
Not the big colonial on Summit.
it turns out. but...

828
00:51:57.323 --> 00:51:58.913
somewhere in that neighborhood.

829
00:51:59.241 --> 00:52:01.541
[chuckling] Asshole abandoned his family.

830
00:52:01.619 --> 00:52:04.159
didn't even have the decency
to move to another fucking town.

831
00:52:04.246 --> 00:52:07.416
Maybe he wants to continue
to be a part of your life.

832
00:52:09.918 --> 00:52:10.918
No.

833
00:52:18.052 --> 00:52:19.182
I look at him

834
00:52:19.261 --> 00:52:23.181
and I look at my grandfather.
and I think. "Where the hell do I end up?"

835
00:52:23.974 --> 00:52:26.234
Wherever you want. I think.

836
00:52:27.353 --> 00:52:28.353
Do you?

837
00:52:29.938 --> 00:52:31.818
Did you end up where you want to be?

838
00:52:32.399 --> 00:52:34.819
Cleaning up coke for a rich white kid.

839
00:52:35.527 --> 00:52:39.567
I'm helping my mother. so.
I'm exactly where I want to be.

840
00:52:40.074 --> 00:52:42.284
Well. fucking good for you.

841
00:52:43.535 --> 00:52:44.535
[scoffs]

842
00:52:45.162 --> 00:52:46.872
Fucking good for you!

843
00:52:49.124 --> 00:52:51.964
- Bryce! That's quite enough.
- Hey. Mom.

844
00:52:53.379 --> 00:52:55.089
[Mrs. Walker] Go to your room. Now!

845
00:52:56.632 --> 00:52:57.802
Guess I'm in trouble.

846
00:52:59.218 --> 00:53:00.218
Good night. Ani.

847
00:53:00.969 --> 00:53:02.509
I'm sorry about the mess.

848
00:53:04.682 --> 00:53:08.062
You are never to speak to her again.
You are not to go near her.

849
00:53:08.143 --> 00:53:10.653
Or you will have no home here.
do you understand me?

850
00:53:10.729 --> 00:53:13.479
- Understand?
- Yes. Yeah. I understand.

851
00:53:20.531 --> 00:53:23.531
I'm so sorry. Mrs. Walker.

852
00:53:24.034 --> 00:53:26.914
Don't be. You did nothing wrong.

853
00:53:26.995 --> 00:53:29.995
He was tired and upset about his father.

854
00:53:30.082 --> 00:53:33.092
Yes. there are all manner of excuses.

855
00:53:34.586 --> 00:53:35.586
But my son...

856
00:53:41.844 --> 00:53:43.304
You should be very careful.

857
00:53:53.355 --> 00:53:55.685
[Ani]<i> That's why I think</i>
<i>it must be hard to be a boy.</i>

858
00:53:57.317 --> 00:53:59.607
<i>Because they still have no idea
what a man is.</i>

859
00:54:01.697 --> 00:54:03.947
- [Amara] Is that comfortable?
- It's fine!

860
00:54:04.491 --> 00:54:05.491
Fine.

861
00:54:10.789 --> 00:54:11.789
Is he awake?

862
00:54:12.207 --> 00:54:14.917
Yes. but he's just taken his medicine.

863
00:54:15.794 --> 00:54:16.804
Excuse me.

864
00:54:17.838 --> 00:54:18.838
Stay.

865
00:54:19.089 --> 00:54:20.089
Please.

866
00:54:21.049 --> 00:54:22.549
This will only take a moment.

867
00:54:28.599 --> 00:54:29.769
Father...

868
00:54:40.319 --> 00:54:41.319
Harrison...

869
00:54:44.198 --> 00:54:45.988
I'm afraid your grandson is dead.

870
00:54:47.493 --> 00:54:49.373
We're attending his funeral tomorrow.

871
00:54:51.121 --> 00:54:52.121
My grandson?

872
00:54:53.582 --> 00:54:54.752
Bryce.

873
00:54:55.626 --> 00:54:56.706
Is dead?

874
00:54:57.419 --> 00:54:58.419
Yes.

875
00:55:00.964 --> 00:55:01.964
What the...

876
00:55:03.258 --> 00:55:05.588
What the hell happened?
What have you done?

877
00:55:05.677 --> 00:55:06.847
Where's Bryce?

878
00:55:07.638 --> 00:55:10.268
He's with the mortician.
being prepared for tomorrow.

879
00:55:10.349 --> 00:55:12.269
What have you done to him?

880
00:55:12.643 --> 00:55:14.023
Dad. please. lie down.

881
00:55:14.102 --> 00:55:16.942
Get the fuck out of my way.
I need to see my grandson!

882
00:55:17.022 --> 00:55:19.072
Where's my cane? Bryce!

883
00:55:19.149 --> 00:55:20.939
Get me my cane. God damn it.

884
00:55:21.026 --> 00:55:23.254
- I need my cane.
- You are not to stand. Doctor's orders.

885
00:55:23.278 --> 00:55:24.278
Where's my cane?

886
00:55:24.363 --> 00:55:27.283
Perhaps if you get him his cane
it will help calm him down.

887
00:55:27.366 --> 00:55:29.826
I had the maid store it
in the carriage house.

888
00:55:29.910 --> 00:55:30.910
Amorowat!

889
00:55:39.586 --> 00:55:41.086
[Ani] <i>Men and their rage...</i>

890
00:55:42.840 --> 00:55:44.300
<i>and their insecurities.</i>

891
00:55:45.050 --> 00:55:46.050
<i>their fears...</i>

892
00:55:47.845 --> 00:55:50.595
<i>and all the things they do
to keep those hidden away.</i>

893
00:56:00.566 --> 00:56:01.566
Wow.

894
00:56:09.867 --> 00:56:13.117
We're sending you back to the future!

895
00:56:28.927 --> 00:56:30.047
[Ani] <i>Alex was right.</i>

896
00:56:31.805 --> 00:56:32.805
<i>Nobody's clean.</i>

897
00:56:38.937 --> 00:56:39.977
What the hell?

898
00:56:40.689 --> 00:56:43.569
["Something I Learned Today" playing]

899
00:56:49.740 --> 00:56:54.200
<i>♪ Something I learned today
Black and white is always gray ♪</i>

900
00:56:54.286 --> 00:56:56.456
<i>♪ Looking through the window pane ♪</i>

901
00:56:56.538 --> 00:57:00.418
[Alex] <i>For help finding crisis resources.</i>
<i>visit 13reasonswhy.info.</i>

902
00:57:09.217 --> 00:57:13.307
<i>♪ Something I learned today
Yield to the right-of-way ♪</i>

903
00:57:13.847 --> 00:57:15.887
<i>♪ Stopping at a four-way sign ♪</i>

904
00:57:15.974 --> 00:57:17.604
<i>♪ Someone else's rules ♪</i>

905
00:57:17.684 --> 00:57:21.694
<i>♪ Oh. not mine ♪</i>

906
00:57:28.528 --> 00:57:33.198
<i>♪ Something I learned today
Never look straight in the sun's rays ♪</i>

907
00:57:33.283 --> 00:57:35.413
<i>♪ Letting all the sunshine in ♪</i>

908
00:57:35.494 --> 00:57:37.834
<i>♪ Can't remember where ♪</i>

909
00:57:37.913 --> 00:57:43.133
<i>♪ I've been ♪</i>

910
00:57:51.218 --> 00:57:55.678
<i>♪ Something I learned today
Something I learned today ♪</i>

911
00:57:55.764 --> 00:57:59.984
<i>♪ Something I learned today
Something I learned today ♪</i>

912
00:58:48.650 --> 00:58:50.400
[man] <i>Well done. Ed. Well done.</i>

